? The bones of Aletopelta were found in California with shells attached to them. This led to the suggestion that after the animal died, its skeleton became the base for THIS. Which instance of THIS has the width of about 150 km?
! The Great Barrier Reef.
/ THIS stands here for a reef. Bivalve mollusc shells attached to the dinosaur skeleton led to the suggestion that the dinosaur had once drowned in a river, and the carcass was then washed out to the sea and became part of a reef. The southern stretch of the Great Barrier Reef has the width of 152 km.
^ 
